# stations.filter - which ALERT addresses get baked into app/alert_stations_gen.h
#
# Consumed by tools/gen_stations.py. The station data itself lives in the MegaNet
# repository (github.com/cdomotor-g/MegaNet); nothing from it is copied into this repo
# except the generated header, which CI regenerates.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SYNTAX
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One directive per line. Blank lines and everything after a '#' are ignored.
# All include directives are OR-combined: an ALERT address is kept if ANY of them match.
# 'exclude ...' directives are applied afterwards and remove addresses that did match.
#
#   range LOW-HIGH        Include every ALERT id in the inclusive range.
#                         e.g.  range 4600-4699
#
#   id N                  Include the single ALERT id N.
#                         e.g.  id 6129
#
#   network <name>        Case-insensitive substring of a radio network. Matches either
#                         a radio_networks name/id in stations.json, or the "BoM Network"
#                         column of data/ALL_REPEATERS.csv - in which case every address
#                         inside that repeater's pass ranges is included. The CSV is the
#                         useful path: stations.json only tags 88 of 3,174 stations with a
#                         radio_network_id, while the pass ranges cover the whole network.
#                         e.g.  network Mt Kanigan
#
#   catchment <name>      Case-insensitive substring of a catchment id or name from
#                         stations.json (drainage basin, e.g. "Fitzroy", "brisbane").
#                         Only stations.json-sourced addresses carry catchments.
#                         e.g.  catchment Burdekin
#
#   station <name>        Case-insensitive substring of the station name.
#                         e.g.  station Caniaview
#
#   all                   Everything MegaNet knows about. ~42 KB of table - far more than
#                         the flash budget allows, so this is only useful with a large
#                         --max-bytes for experiments.
#
#   exclude range LOW-HIGH
#   exclude station <name>
#   exclude network <name>
#   exclude catchment <name>
#   exclude id N          Remove matches after the includes have been applied.
#
# Handy commands:
#   python3 tools/gen_stations.py --meganet-dir ../MegaNet --list-networks
#       prints every network and catchment with its station count, address count and
#       estimated table cost in bytes - use it to plan a filter that fits.
#   python3 tools/gen_stations.py --meganet-dir ../MegaNet
#       regenerates app/alert_stations_gen.h and prints the resulting size.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DEFAULT SET, AND WHY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Budget: the firmware overflowed flash, so --max-bytes is now 6400 (was 8000) and the
# table must come in at or under it. 'all' is 42,380 bytes (2,579 sites / 5,283 addresses),
# so it is not an option.
#
# Names now also drop a trailing "AL"/"ALERT" marker ("Loudoun Br AL" -> "LOUDOUN BR"),
# which shortened the name pool and took roughly 5% off every figure below.
#
# Per-network cost, from --list-networks (bytes = 6 * sites + name pool):
#
#     Constitution Hill        389 stations    922 addrs    6767 bytes
#     Mt Kanigan               322 stations    733 addrs    5530 bytes
#     Mt Stuart                171 stations    420 addrs    2950 bytes
#     Emerald                  140 stations    308 addrs    2401 bytes
#     Saddle Mt                 84 stations    203 addrs    1483 bytes
#     Oakey Met Office          63 stations    150 addrs    1095 bytes
#     Gladstone                 56 stations    144 addrs     986 bytes
#     Mackay Met Office         56 stations    139 addrs     968 bytes
#     Rockhampton Met Office    55 stations    131 addrs     977 bytes
#     Charleville Met Office    52 stations    119 addrs     874 bytes
#     Mt Glorious (SEQWater)    39 stations     91 addrs     692 bytes
#     Blackall                  13 stations     29 addrs     210 bytes
#     Barcaldine                 8 stations     21 addrs     115 bytes
#     Marburg                    1 station       2 addrs      19 bytes
#     Mt Stapylton               1 station       2 addrs      18 bytes
#
# Picked greedily by station count: take the biggest network that still fits, repeat.
# Constitution Hill (South East Queensland) is the biggest at 389 stations but costs 6,767
# bytes - it no longer fits on its own even after the "AL" stripping, so it is skipped.
# Mt Kanigan (322 stations, 5,530) is the largest that fits; of the remaining 870 bytes,
# Charleville Met Office would need 6,404 total (4 bytes over) and Blackall 6,432, so the
# next ones that fit are Mt Glorious (SEQWater), Barcaldine, and the two single-station
# networks Marburg and Mt Stapylton.
#
#     Mt Kanigan + Mt Glorious (SEQWater) + Barcaldine + Marburg + Mt Stapylton
#       -> 379 sites, 849 addresses, 371 stations, 6,374 bytes (26 to spare)
#
# To retarget the firmware at a different region, comment these out and pick another set
# from the table above. Sets that also fit under 6,400:
#     Mt Stuart + Emerald + Gladstone            392 sites, 871 addrs, 6,323 bytes
#     Mt Stuart + Emerald + Charleville Met Off.               approx 6,225 bytes
#     Mt Kanigan + Mt Glorious (SEQWater)        369 sites, 824 addrs, 6,222 bytes
# Constitution Hill only fits if --max-bytes is raised back to 6,800 or more.

network Mt Kanigan
network Mt Glorious
network Barcaldine
network Marburg
network Mt Stapylton
